now  he said that um we've already procured  enough vaccine doses  to begin booster shots later this year  and  they're going to be working with the  current vaccine supplies and new  suppliers  like the cure vac partnership to work  out which vaccines will be effective as  a booster shot  and he talked about specifically  designing vaccines for  uh variants of concerns such as the  south african  variants now of course the announcement  about the  indian indian red list  move came hours after the prime minister  confirmed what many of us suspected that  his trip to uh  uh india big trade trip with all sorts  of trade deals he wanted to do  post-brexit due a week a week today  next week that's off this was the prime  minister confirming that today  narendra modi and i have uh have  basically come to the conclusion that  very sadly i won't be able to  uh to go ahead with the trip i do think  it's only sensible uh  to postpone given what's happening uh in  india the  the shape of the pandemic uh there we're  gonna we're gonna be going back and the  relationship between the uk  and india is of huge importance and i'll  be talking to narendra modi on promise  modi  on monday we'll be doing we're trying to  do as much as we can  virtually  well the cancelling of this india trip  uh begs questions what about some of the  other big international uh  events the prime minister's due to take  place to part in  later this year there's the g7 summit  down at a hotel down in cornwall  is that going to go ahead as planned uh  with all the  international travel involved in that  and then of course the cop 26 uh  summit on the environment climate change  due to happening glasgow later in the  year  now the copper president that's alex  sharma former cabinet minister  insisted in the commons the other day it  would go ahead  in person with everybody coming into  glasgow for that  but there are some doubts about that as  well whilst there are all these variants  in places like south 